{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You are to die, etc.</b> Meaning: you are liable to death for taking her, etc. — that is, after I inform you that she is a married woman. But if they had not informed him, even though he would have committed the act, he would not be liable to death, for a descendant of Noah who lies with another man's wife unintentionally, thinking she is unmarried, is exempt, as Rambam wrote in chapter 10 of Hilkhot Melakhim." "Further, the verse may bear this reading: <b>You are to die</b>, etc., <b>whom you have taken, she being a married woman</b> — meaning, even though you knew she was a married woman, and accordingly he would be liable according to the law. However, the truth of the matter, from what is stated in the narrative, appears to be that he did not know she was a married woman."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:25.134216623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}